Third-party material
--------------------

This product contains material derived from Cuberite
(https://github.com/cuberite/cuberite, https://cuberite.org),
Copyright 2011-2025 Cuberite Contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The following parts of this plugin were written by reading Cuberite's source
and mirroring its behaviour; they are derivative works of the files listed:

  * decay.lua - leaf decay rules
    Mirrors src/Blocks/BlockLeaves.h (cBlockLeavesHandler):
      - the survival rule: a leaves block lives while a log can be reached by
        walking at most LEAVES_CHECK_DISTANCE (= 6) leaves blocks;
      - player-placed leaves identified by meta bit 0x04 are left alone;
      - meta bit 0x08 is the "needs a decay check" flag, which the plugin clears
        on leaves it has already proven to be in reach of a log;
      - vanilla drop probabilities for saplings, sticks and apples
        (sapling 1/20, jungle sapling 1/40, apple 1/200, sticks 1/50 counting
        1-2 items), applied through the server's own block handler.

  * decay.lua - vine support rules
    Re-implements src/Blocks/BlockVines.h (cBlockVinesHandler):
      - IsBlockAttachable(): a block is a vine support unless it is one of the
        glass/chest/piston family, otherwise cBlockInfo::IsSolid() decides;
      - GetMaxMeta(): the side bits of the vine meta, the "solid block above"
        rule and the "vine above shares a side bit" rule.
    This re-implementation exists because GetMaxMeta() returns VINE_UNCHANGED
    whenever "meta & maxMeta == meta", which is always true for a vine whose
    meta has already been reduced to 0 - such a vine is never destroyed, so
    leaves floating vines behind once the canopy is gone.

  * decay.lua, selftest.lua - block update semantics
    Verified against src/Chunk.cpp (cChunk::SetBlock queues the position for
    the neighbour check that cChunk::CheckBlocks() runs each tick) and
    src/Blocks/BlockHandler.cpp (cBlockHandler::Check() notifies all six
    neighbours), which is why removing leaves through
    cWorld::DropBlockAsPickups() wakes up dependent blocks such as vines.

  * selftest.lua - the 6-step distance boundary and the 68-leaves canopy layout
    were derived from reading the cBlockLeavesHandler::HasNearLog() search and
    from Cuberite's own LEAVES_CHECK_DISTANCE constant.

No Cuberite source file is copied verbatim into this repository; only the
behaviour listed above was re-implemented in Lua.
